{"id": "EUVD-2026-103901", "enisaUuid": "9f7d615b-e442-3237-8c93-694bac9a4ee8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Fix overflow of jump offset in constant blinding\n\nbpf_jit_blind_insn() rewrites 'if rX op imm goto off' into:\n\n  AX = imm ^ rnd\n  AX ^= rnd\n  if rX op AX goto off\n\nand subtracts 2 from off when the jump is backward. off is s16, so\n-32767 and -32768 wrap and the jump goes 32767 insns forward, past the\nend of the prog. The jump is inside the patch, hence bpf_adj_branches()\ndoesn't check it. The kernel crashes when such prog runs with\nbpf_jit_harden=2.\n\nReturn -ERANGE in such case. bpf_jit_blind_constants() fails the same\nway when blinding of other insns moves a jump out of range.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:49:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:26:09", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/443328237113ee0ea515e506497334d871dbc2aa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ad139384ecddb6f3e7e3c3c12765aafae0e39670"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6x96-v5fq-fjjw", "CVE-2026-98816"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05d60ecd-5d7c-309b-9003-f8d552e3ff9e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "93c557cb-4aaa-3a4e-888c-a5e9b6d6e491", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "b3e0ec79-b707-3b65-aa68-914ea5341dec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b561a9f1-8be8-3585-8330-5fe85d70cbb9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f3446bb809f20ad56cadf712e6006815ae7a8f9 <443328237113ee0ea515e506497334d871dbc2aa"}, {"id": "db9068d0-42ba-3d90-a9df-9be8b1be86cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f3446bb809f20ad56cadf712e6006815ae7a8f9 <ad139384ecddb6f3e7e3c3c12765aafae0e39670"}, {"id": "fc9b311a-6217-3330-945b-7e99c154ee9b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "32904270-05cd-307b-aaf8-cca3e87065cb", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}